/-! ### A genuine odd-order stationary lower bound

The quadratic stationary package in `Auxiliary` already contains the exact
one-step recurrence at the first odd moment.  Unlike the order-zero Fresnel
term, this recurrence has an explicit nonzero boundary coefficient.  The
following lemma turns that coefficient and the proved `O(lambda^(-1/2))`
bound for the derivative remainder into a quantitative eventual lower bound.

This is the first analytic lower estimate needed by the BRRS shell packet:
it applies, in particular, to the `d = 3` meridional endpoint.  It is kept
generic so that the odd-order recurrence can be iterated in a subsequent
development. -/

/-- The nonzero leading coefficient produced by iterating the odd quadratic
endpoint recurrence.  The recurrence is kept rather than expanded into
factorials so its phase and normalization remain transparent. -/
